<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Nile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Aboukir Bay · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> was a naval battle fought on 1–3 August 1798 in Aboukir Bay, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. A British fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> attacked the French fleet that had carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s army to Egypt, destroying or capturing eleven of its thirteen ships of the line, including the flagship L'Orient, which exploded. The victory stranded the French army in Egypt and restored British naval dominance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-nile.jpg" alt="Battle of the Nile" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Arnald · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_the_Nile.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The American War of Independence ended in defeat after the surrender at Yorktown in 1781, but from 1793 Britain led coalitions against revolutionary France, and Horatio Nelson destroyed a French fleet at the <b>Battle of the Nile</b> in 1798.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>He landed at Alexandria in July, defeated the Mamluk beys at the Battle of the Pyramids and entered Cairo, but Nelson destroyed his fleet at <b>Aboukir Bay</b> in August 1798.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-occupation-of-egypt">French occupation of Egypt</a></li></ul></section>
